> Two bridi can be connected by {i SUMTCITA bo}. {bo} has two effects: it
> prevents an immediately following sumti from being taken as the object of
> the
> preposition, and it groups the bridi more tightly and right-associatively
> than
> surrounding bridi connected by just {i}. One may want left-association:
>
> lo filso cu lacpu lo mamta bakni lo carce .icabo lo cifybakni cu pinfu
> .itezu'ebo facki lo jei la .iaves. kau gasnu lo nunbilma
>
> (This is an abbreviated version of 1 Samuel 6:7-9.) Is there a way to
> connect
> three or more bridi with prepositions without forcing right association?
>


Won't {iJA TAG bo} fix the problem?

Or by not using {i TAG bo} at all, fix the scope by moving the
prepositional phrases to the right and join them using {ce'e} or {e}.


